{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared vocabulary for the CSM language files. Two jobs:",
    "  1. `protected` lists strings that must survive translation untouched. They are swapped",
    "     for sentinels around each API call and restored afterwards, the same mechanism the",
    "     launcher's translate-locales.js uses for {0} placeholders.",
    "  2. `terms` pins the translation of vocabulary that recurs across many names. A machine",
    "     translator has no memory between calls, so without this the same English head noun",
    "     comes back three different ways in three different places -- invisible to anyone who",
    "     does not read the language. Any English term listed here is substituted directly and",
    "     never sent to the API.",
    "These values were settled during the bulk translation pass; keep them in step with it."
  ],

  "protected": [
    "EST", "Wheelock", "Simplex", "SpectrAlert", "Gentex", "TrueAlert", "Genesis",
    "Adaptahorn", "Integrity", "NOV", "GreenCobra", "DuraLife", "MacLean", "PUPI",
    "McCain", "Econolite", "Autoscope", "Solo Terra", "Miovision", "Campbell", "Guardian",
    "Polara", "iN2", "Barlo", "KAC", "Kidde", "JBL", "Bose", "Verizon", "Lithonia",
    "Leotek", "Westinghouse", "Solarmax", "Verifone", "TP-Link", "Omada", "Enterasys",
    "Spectrum", "Technicolor", "American Electric", "Etch A Sketch", "Apple", "iPhone",
    "iPad", "iMac", "MacBook", "GE", "MBTA", "MassDOT", "LADOT", "Alto", "UIA", "DWP",
    "FAWE", "RGR",
    "HOV", "FYA", "MPH", "FDC", "ARV", "ATV", "LED", "HVAC", "CSM", "TV", "APS", "ISA",
    "GCM", "LF", "HWY", "FWY", "JCT", "PCH", "LHS"
  ],

  "_units_note": [
    "Units printed on the depicted sign face stay verbatim, because a localised label would",
    "contradict the artwork the player is looking at: MPH, clock times such as 8:30a-5:30p,",
    "and distances such as 500 Feet / 1 Mile. Units that are equipment specifications and",
    "appear on no sign are localised instead: lens diameters in inches, rotation in degrees.",
    "The sign-face units are listed in `protected` or matched by `signFaceUnitPattern`."
  ],
  "signFaceUnitPattern": "\\b(MPH|Feet|Foot|Miles?)\\b|\\d{1,2}:\\d{2}\\s*[ap]\\b",

